--[[
================================================================================

        S C A N N E R S        (ObjectScanner)

        DOORS' two scanners, the one you pick, in your inventory and working:

            Nokia     DOORS' own scanner (the Mines'): its model, its icon, its
                      animations
            Tablet    the NVCS tablet (the model of the tablet's own script):
                      it sees the room through its screen

        Each in three versions: Normal, Guiding Light (blue) and Curious Light
        (yellow), with their glow. Their icon is their own: in a Light, or in
        a colour of yours, the same icon with its screen in that colour (made
        once from assets/scanner/, kept in ObjectScanner/Icons/).

            _G.Scanner = { Type = "Tablet", Variant = "Guiding" }   -- optional
            loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bonellocristian78-lab/Gradish-Mode/main/ObjectScanner"))()

        Type       "Scanner" (the Nokia: the default), "Tablet"
        Variant    "Normal" (the default), "Guiding", "Curious"
        Color      its screen: "Red", "Orange", "Yellow", "Lime", "Green", "Cyan",
                   "Blue", "Purple", "Pink", "White" (or any Color3); by default
                   its own, or the Light's
        FPS        how many times a second its screen is drawn (30, as DOORS')

        In your hand:
            Left click   turn it on / off      (in SNAKE: turn left)
            Right click  inspect it            (in SNAKE: turn right)
            F            the next function
            L            a trick: it flies, it spins, it falls...
            X            drop it (E to pick it up)

        Its functions (F): SCANNER (DOORS' own: what is worth finding),
        ENTITIES (what is coming, and from where), EXIT (an arrow to the next
        door), HIDING (where to hide), TRAPS (fake doors, snares, Giggles); and
        its own: the Nokia SNAKE, the Tablet X-RAY.

        Run it again to change it: the old one goes away. Its battery never
        runs out.

================================================================================
]]

